 ],
 "timeline": [
  {
   "turn_index": 0,
   "speaker": "Beatrice",
   "text": "Good evening. Let's start with the hall and the menu. Oren, how are tickets?",
   "start_s": 0.5,
   "end_s": 6.293
  },
  {
   "turn_index": 1,
   "speaker": "Oren",
   "text": "A hundred and twelve sold, at a hundred and twenty-five each.",
   "start_s": 7.449,
   "end_s": 11.574
  },
  {
   "turn_index": 2,
   "speaker": "Beatrice",
   "text": "And the hall holds a hundred and eighty, so there's room.",
   "start_s": 12.722,
   "end_s": 17.274
  },
  {
   "turn_index": 3,
   "speaker": "Desmond",
   "text": "The menu is forty-eight a head. The caterer needs a final number two weeks out.",
   "start_s": 17.531,
   "end_s": 24.197
  },
  {
   "turn_index": 4,
   "speaker": "Fumiko",
   "text": "Do we order for the tickets sold, or for the hall?",
   "start_s": 24.482,
   "end_s": 28.882
  },
  {
   "turn_index": 5,
   "speaker": "Desmond",
   "text": "For the tickets sold, plus ten percent. That's what we did last year.",
   "start_s": 29.917,
   "end_s": 35.695
  },
  {
   "turn_index": 6,
   "speaker": "Oren",
   "text": "The hall used to be a cannery, you know. My grandfather worked the line there in the fifties.",
   "start_s": 36.631,
   "end_s": 43.381
  },
  {
   "turn_index": 7,
   "speaker": "Beatrice",
   "text": "I didn't know that. How lovely.",
   "start_s": 44.251,
   "end_s": 46.733
  },
  {
   "turn_index": 8,
   "speaker": "Fumiko",
   "text": "Is there a vegetarian option this year? Several people asked.",
   "start_s": 47.241,
   "end_s": 51.241
  },
  {
   "turn_index": 9,
   "speaker": "Desmond",
   "text": "The squash risotto. The caterer says it's popular.",
   "start_s": 52.047,
   "end_s": 55.602
  },
  {
   "turn_index": 10,
   "speaker": "Beatrice",
   "text": "Then we'll order on tickets sold plus ten percent, with the risotto as the vegetarian main.",
   "start_s": 56.409,
   "end_s": 63.029
  },
  {
   "turn_index": 11,
   "speaker": "Fumiko",
   "text": "Good.",
   "start_s": 63.81,
   "end_s": 64.21
  },
  {
   "turn_index": 12,
   "speaker": "Beatrice",
   "text": "The auction. Oren?",
   "start_s": 64.568,
   "end_s": 65.81
  },
  {
   "turn_index": 13,
   "speaker": "Oren",
   "text": "We're at about forty items. Some lovely ones, too.",
   "start_s": 66.441,
   "end_s": 69.816
  },
  {
   "turn_index": 14,
   "speaker": "Fumiko",
   "text": "I have the intake sheet here. It's thirty-one that have actually arrived.",
   "start_s": 70.41,
   "end_s": 75.21
  },
  {
   "turn_index": 15,
   "speaker": "Oren",
   "text": "Thirty-one in hand, and about nine more promised. Fair point.",
   "start_s": 76.133,
   "end_s": 79.883
  },
  {
   "turn_index": 16,
   "speaker": "Desmond",
   "text": "What's the best item so far?",
   "start_s": 81.078,
   "end_s": 83.744
  },
  {
   "turn_index": 17,
   "speaker": "Oren",
   "text": "The guided canoe trip on the reserve. And the hand-made quilt from the Hendersons.",
   "start_s": 84.893,
   "end_s": 90.143
  },
  {
   "turn_index": 18,
   "speaker": "Beatrice",
   "text": "Should we put the quilt in a live auction instead of the silent one?",
   "start_s": 90.887,
   "end_s": 96.68
  },
  {
   "turn_index": 19,
   "speaker": "Oren",
   "text": "It might do better live. One live item is a nice moment in the evening.",
   "start_s": 97.325,
   "end_s": 102.95
  },
  {
   "turn_index": 20,
   "speaker": "Desmond",
   "text": "Who'd run the live part? We don't have an auctioneer.",
   "start_s": 103.418,
   "end_s": 107.863
  },
  {
   "turn_index": 21,
   "speaker": "Beatrice",
   "text": "I could do it. I've done it at the school before.",
   "start_s": 108.099,
   "end_s": 112.651
  },
  {
   "turn_index": 22,
   "speaker": "Oren",
   "text": "That would be perfect.",
   "start_s": 112.878,
   "end_s": 114.378
  },
  {
   "turn_index": 23,
   "speaker": "Fumiko",
   "text": "It might help if someone chased the nine promised items this week.",
   "start_s": 115.043,
   "end_s": 119.843
  },
  {
   "turn_index": 24,
   "speaker": "Oren",
   "text": "I'll call the nine donors on Monday and confirm drop-off dates.",
   "start_s": 120.361,
   "end_s": 124.486
  },
  {
   "turn_index": 25,
   "speaker": "Beatrice",
   "text": "Sponsors. Desmond?",
   "start_s": 125.066,
   "end_s": 125.894
  },
  {
   "turn_index": 26,
   "speaker": "Desmond",
   "text": "Five sponsors, fourteen thousand five hundred in total.",
   "start_s": 126.986,
   "end_s": 130.541
  },
  {
   "turn_index": 27,
   "speaker": "Oren",
   "text": "The goal for the evening is sixty thousand.",
   "start_s": 131.267,
   "end_s": 134.267
  },
  {
   "turn_index": 28,
   "speaker": "Beatrice",
   "text": "Last year we raised fifty-eight thousand, so sixty is within reach.",
   "start_s": 135.028,
   "end_s": 139.579
  },
  {
   "turn_index": 29,
   "speaker": "Fumiko",
   "text": "My neighbor just put solar panels on her whole roof. She says her bill is nearly zero.",
   "start_s": 140.015,
   "end_s": 146.815
  },
  {
   "turn_index": 30,
   "speaker": "Desmond",
   "text": "My brother-in-law is thinking about it. The installers are booked for months.",
   "start_s": 147.039,
   "end_s": 152.372
  },
  {
   "turn_index": 31,
   "speaker": "Oren",
   "text": "Could we ask the solar company to sponsor? It fits what we do.",
   "start_s": 152.897,
   "end_s": 157.772
  },
  {
   "turn_index": 32,
   "speaker": "Beatrice",
   "text": "That's a good thought. Let's think about it for next year, since the program is printed already.",
   "start_s": 158.109,
   "end_s": 165.143
  },
  {
   "turn_index": 33,
   "speaker": "Desmond",
   "text": "Has anyone heard back from the bank about renewing their sponsorship?",
   "start_s": 165.853,
   "end_s": 170.742
  },
  {
   "turn_index": 34,
   "speaker": "Oren",
   "text": "The brewery wants to donate the beer instead of cash. Is that okay?",
   "start_s": 171.941,
   "end_s": 176.816
  },
  {
   "turn_index": 35,
   "speaker": "Desmond",
   "text": "That's fine. In-kind counts, I just record it differently.",
   "start_s": 177.69,
   "end_s": 181.69
  },
  {
   "turn_index": 36,
   "speaker": "Beatrice",
   "text": "Volunteers. Fumiko?",
   "start_s": 182.072,
   "end_s": 182.899
  },
  {
   "turn_index": 37,
   "speaker": "Fumiko",
   "text": "We need twenty and we have thirteen.",
   "start_s": 183.993,
   "end_s": 186.793
  },
  {
   "turn_index": 38,
   "speaker": "Oren",
   "text": "Seven short. Where are the gaps?",
   "start_s": 187.79,
   "end_s": 190.04
  },
  {
   "turn_index": 39,
   "speaker": "Fumiko",
   "text": "Setup in the afternoon, and cleanup at the end. Nobody wants cleanup.",
   "start_s": 190.974,
   "end_s": 195.774
  },
  {
   "turn_index": 40,
   "speaker": "Desmond",
   "text": "I'll do cleanup. I'm always last to leave anyway.",
   "start_s": 196.881,
   "end_s": 200.881
  },
  {
   "turn_index": 41,
   "speaker": "Beatrice",
   "text": "Could we ask the high school's environmental club? They need service hours.",
   "start_s": 201.844,
   "end_s": 206.809
  },
  {
   "turn_index": 42,
   "speaker": "Fumiko",
   "text": "That's a good idea. I'll email their teacher tomorrow.",
   "start_s": 207.799,
   "end_s": 211.399
  },
  {
   "turn_index": 43,
   "speaker": "Beatrice",
   "text": "Then Desmond has cleanup, and we ask the club to cover setup.",
   "start_s": 211.953,
   "end_s": 216.918
  },
  {
   "turn_index": 44,
   "speaker": "Oren",
   "text": "And the date's still October fourth for everyone, right? A sponsor asked me.",
   "start_s": 218.099,
   "end_s": 222.974
  },
  {
   "turn_index": 45,
   "speaker": "Beatrice",
   "text": "October fourth. Nothing's changed. Thank you, everyone. A lovely meeting.",
   "start_s": 224.136,
   "end_s": 228.274
  }
 ]
}